<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to buy 32,000/T jet A-1 in 2H Feb.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to buy 32,000/T jet A-1 in 2H Feb.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to buy 32,000 tonnes of jet A-1 for delivery February 15-28, a company official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender, which closes January 13 and is valid for two days, seeks offers on a cost-and-freight basis to Shen Ao or Keelung.</p>
<p>CPC's last purchase of jet fuel was around $270 per tonne c-and-f Taiwan, for delivery in the second half of January.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
